{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/189769-best-of-both-worlds-and-beyond","id":189769,"title":"Best of both worlds and beyond ...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-06T18:54:02-07:00","id":189769,"title":"Best of both worlds and beyond ...","content":"I have an ex because they wanted all the privileges of the 1890s and 1990s with none of the responsibilities of either. However, with WoD, it seems to me that it just might be possible to manage that rare thing - the best of both worlds. How much of the discussion here is on how to maintain the best of CWoD using NWoD improvements, and continuing to improve from there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T19:37:55-07:00","id":189821,"title":"","content":"Well, considering that there's three published supplements (Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage, and a Demon one on the way) that help convert the cosmologies and mechanics between WoDs, I'd say it's a pretty healthy subject of discussion. I recently played a Technocracy game featuring <b>Mage: The Awakening</b> / <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b> rules, and felt that the alternate mechanics greatly added to the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T19:49:06-07:00","id":189826,"title":"","content":"I am enjoying some of the game mechanic changes - just not the cosmogony with which they seem bagged. And it is not that the writers aren't working very hard on their writing of it. Asimov had wonderful basic ideas, but I didn't like is stuff either. So they are in good company and I mean them no disrespect. Right now, I am writing a background story for my ideas for a new approach to Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T05:19:55-07:00","id":193403,"title":"","content":"Will you be sharing or otherwise posting online this different approach to Wraith? I'm quite interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T04:10:36-07:00","id":196181,"title":"","content":"Certainly, however, atm I am having a bit of writers block. I need specific dialogue to go with my opening story line as I am working up the structure.<br /> <br /> Here is a part of my opening fiction:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He crouches lower, listening in vain for the silent wings hunting him. Sweat pours down his face, his back, across the palms of his hands. He can sense it again, just as the rabbit can sense the cat. It's close. Queasiness forms in his stomach. It rises, spreading, growing, seeping up to the back of his skull. The talons suddenly clench into his hunkered down shoulders! He lurches ...<br /> <br /> Damian lurches out of bed. He half rolls half stumbles to his feet and flings himself into the bathroom. There he fills the bowl with several volleys of bile, and rolls off his heels to slump against the cool tub in the neon dark of early night. <br /> <br /> The nightmares are getting worse. Why? Work is fine. Not even a nasty homicide lately. Hell, if I was gonna have nightmares why not be back at Korangal? I've never even seen a real owl. What the hell is my problem? As he forces calm after yet another failed night's sleep the alarm blares in the other room. &quot;Well, time to get ready for patrol,&quot; Officer Raynor said to no one in particular. </div> </div> </div>It is inspired in part from a book I read (in a college course on Death and Dying) called I Heard the Owl Call My Name, by Margaret Craven.<br /> <br /> By the time I get through, as the character enters the Shadowrealms, a spirit of Owl will dive down and with razor sharp talons pull the character back through to the skinlands just in time to keep them from being rent from the caul and taken by other wraiths. From there the character must find their own way into the house to which they are called by Owl: Augurs, Cupids, Custodians, Intercessors, Legionnaires, Medicis, and Scholars. The houses represent the concepts of Portents, Desire, Justice, Purity, War, Healing, and Knowledge. Each is associated with one to three of the original wraith guilds. At that point they are wraiths trapped in the skinlands, with a requirement to address issues which concern their house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T17:45:13-07:00","id":197282,"title":"","content":"Your idea is interesting Whithers, though it feels very out of context. Maybe I just need to go through the entire Wraith system again. I'm almost ready to do so I think. <br /> <br /> I can't say how likely it is to improve Wraith with CWoD rules and still have it look and feel like Wraith as the rest know it. I would direct you to the Ask the Deadguy thread, however, Mr. Dansky doesn't always answer even the most serious of a person's burning questions nor does he give any indication that what your asking will be covered in W20. When given a choice between a serious system question and answering a silly one, he will answer the silly one only. If he answers serious questions it's with brevity and vagueness. Anything you create for Wraith will be your own homebrew improvement. Good Luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T18:43:38-07:00","id":197302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/189769-best-of-both-worlds-and-beyond?p=197282#post197282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your idea is interesting Whithers, though it feels very out of context. Maybe I just need to go through the entire Wraith system again. I'm almost ready to do so I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is largely out of context. WtO asked the question: If you are the victim of an extreme trauma, how do you overcome the shadows of that trauma and transcend to the light? Within that context the entire game followed with the Wraith/Shadow struggle paramount. The context of what I am calling Wraith Unremitting is somewhat closer to Geist in that the question of purpose is not internal, but external. The Augurs become prophets of the dead dealing with omens and portents. The Cupids deal with issues of desire: envy, greed, hope, love, lust, etc. The nature of their character and their death feed into issue to which they are bound. Not because the issue is important for their transcendence, but because the character cannot resolve the questions. What does it mean to be purified or corrupt? When does an Intercessor use their skills to transform the mark (Scrooge?) and when do they go terminator?<br /> \u200b<br /> But you are correct, my intent is to include the dead in the Skinlands, which abandons the segregation imposed in WtO.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}